308	     * TODO: expose commission ledger entries as a sibling endpoint so brands
309	     * can reconcile "why is this payout $X?" against individual commission
310	     * rows. The CommissionLedgerEntry model, commerce.commission_ledger_entries
311	     * table, and CommissionPayoutService already exist — the only thing
312	     * missing is the HTTP layer (controller method + route + resource + test).
313	     * Deferred until a real brand asks; when promoting, decide between:
314	     *   a) nested under a specific payout ID (GET /stripe/payouts/{id}/entries)
315	     *      — simplest, answers the "reconcile this one payout" question.
316	     *   b) a top-level list with filter params (GET /stripe/commissions?
317	     *      payout_id=&date_from=&date_to=&status=) — more flexible but more
318	     *      surface area to validate.
